# ---- Environment ----
# Real environment files never enter the repository; the *.example templates always must, because
# the deployment procedure starts by copying one (deploy/DEPLOYMENT.md §2). The broad `.env.*`
# rule swallows `.env.production.example` too, so it needs its own negation — without it the
# documented first step of a production deploy refers to a file that was never committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
!backend/.env.example

# ---- IDE ----
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# ---- Node / Frontend (added in Module 2) ----
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
# The bare `lib/` rule above (Python build dir) must not swallow the frontend's app code.
!frontend/src/lib/

# ---- Logs / runtime ----
*.log
logs/
*.sqlite3
*.db

# ---- OS ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Docker volumes (local) ----
docker/data/

# ---- Competitor reference captures ----
# REPOSITORY_RULES.md requires the AiSensy capture archive to stay local and never be staged,
# committed or bundled. Without this rule a `git add -A` commits the whole archive.
.reference/
